# Milestone: M3
# Covers: a strand created in DORMANT state is not dispatched until
#         urbi_strand_start transitions it to READY; after start it runs.
#
# blocked: T39 host-driver not implemented
# matrix-row: scheduler-strand
#
# Reason: requires Strand.new urbiscript binding to create a strand in
# DORMANT state and then start it.  The chk runner is REPL-driven and has
# no way to express the create-then-start sequence from urbiscript alone
# at M3.  T39 introduces the ## host: driver; T20-promotion exposes
# Strand.new at the urbiscript level.
#
# When T39 + T20-promotion land, implement this fixture by:
#   ## host: s = urbi_strand_create(vm, realm, body_chunk)
#   ## host: assert s->state == USTRAND_STATE_DORMANT
#   ## host: urbi_strand_start(s)
#   ## host: step until quiescent
#   --- expected output (body_chunk prints "ran") ---
#   [00000001] "ran"
